From cb7abea6131023cd1ffdd4e493bf0e74d6999e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:59:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 70/94] iio: common: qcom_smgr: accept NAK_REPORT_ID on an ADD
 as stock does

The AckNak check took NAK_REPORT_ID (3) as success only for a DELETE
and as a refusal for an ADD. The stock sensors HAL never counts it as
an error, whatever the action and the result: in
SMGRSensor::processBufferingResp an error is a non-zero result or an
AckNak above ACK_MODIFIED, unless the AckNak is NAK_REPORT_ID. Should
this firmware answer an ADD with it, say on a sampling_frequency write
while streaming, the write failed and the fallback sent up to 34 more
ADDs, each answered the same way and each logged as a refusal, while
the report probably kept running.

Accept it for an ADD too, at debug level, as for a DELETE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 21 +++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index 0f7f601b0..b79394dd4 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -288,10 +288,13 @@ static unsigned int qcom_smgr_samples_per_report(const struct qcom_smgr_sensor *
 }
 
 /*
- * Turn the AckNak of a buffering response into an error code. ACK_MODIFIED
- * means SMGR substituted a parameter and runs the report anyway; the stock
- * HAL logs it only at debug level, so does this. NAK_REPORT_ID answers a
- * DELETE of a report SMGR does not have, which is what the DELETE wanted.
+ * Turn the AckNak of a buffering response into an error code, as the stock
+ * HAL does (SMGRSensor::processBufferingResp): ACK_SUCCESS and ACK_MODIFIED
+ * are accepted unless the result says otherwise; ACK_MODIFIED means SMGR
+ * substituted a parameter and runs the report anyway, which stock logs only
+ * at debug level, so does this. NAK_REPORT_ID ("no such report") is never
+ * an error to stock, whatever the result, for an ADD as for a DELETE; for a
+ * DELETE it means the report is gone, which is what the DELETE wanted.
  */
 static int qcom_smgr_check_buffering_resp(struct qcom_smgr *smgr,
 					  struct qcom_smgr_sensor *sensor,
@@ -309,12 +312,14 @@ static int qcom_smgr_check_buffering_resp(struct qcom_smgr *smgr,
 			sensor->id, sample_rate, reason);
 		break;
 	case SNS_SMGR_RESPONSE_NAK_REPORT_ID:
-		if (!enable) {
+		if (enable)
+			dev_dbg(smgr->dev,
+				"0x%02x: %u Hz report: no such report, result 0x%x, accepted\n",
+				sensor->id, sample_rate, resp->result);
+		else
 			dev_dbg(smgr->dev, "0x%02x: no report to delete\n",
 				sensor->id);
-			return 0;
-		}
-		fallthrough;
+		return 0;
 	default:
 		if (enable)
 			dev_warn(smgr->dev,
